@startuml
actor Automobiliste
boundary Interface
participant "pieces.js Service (Frontend)" as PiecesService
control "pieceController (Backend)" as PieceController
control "pieceService (Backend)" as PieceService
participant "utils/algorithms.js" as Algorithms
database "Base de données" as DB

ref over Automobiliste, Interface, PiecesService, PieceController, PieceService, DB : Authentification (optionnelle pour lecture)

' Catalogue - listing
Automobiliste -> Interface : 1: Ouvrir catalogue pièces
Interface -> PiecesService : 1.1: listerPieces(page,limit,search,sort)
PiecesService -> PieceController : GET /api/pieces?params
PieceController -> PieceService : getPieces(params)
PieceService -> DB : SELECT ... FROM pieces WHERE ... LIMIT/OFFSET
DB --> PieceService : rows
PieceService --> PieceController : liste_pieces + métadonnées
PieceController --> PiecesService : 200 OK { pieces, total, page, limit }
PiecesService --> Interface : rendre la liste (filtres actifs)
Interface --> Automobiliste : affichage catalogue

' Comparaison multi‑vendeurs
Automobiliste -> Interface : 2: Demande comparaison (nom ou pieceId)
Interface -> PiecesService : 2.1: comparePieceAcrossVendors(params)
PiecesService -> PieceController : GET /api/pieces/compare/vendors?name=...&pieceId=...
PieceController -> PieceService : comparePieceAcrossVendors({ pieceId, name, includeOutOfStock })
note right of PieceService: Implémente logique de comparaison
note right of PieceService: - SELECT offres (JOIN users)
note right of PieceService: - Calcul des stats prix (min,max,avg)
note right of PieceService: - Construction du résumé et des offres triées
PieceService -> DB : SELECT * FROM pieces WHERE ... ORDER BY prix_unitaire ASC
DB --> PieceService : offres
PieceService --> PieceController : 200 OK { piece, offres, summary }
PieceController --> PiecesService : 200 OK { comparison data }
PiecesService --> Interface : afficher tableau comparatif
Interface --> Automobiliste : comparaison affichée

' Remarque: scoring/algorithmes
note left of Algorithms
  `backend/utils/algorithms.js` contient
  fonctions de scoring (haversine, calculateGarageScore,
  calculateInterventionScore) utilisées par les
  endpoints de garages / matching.
end note

@enduml
